Return value onRowsRendered : (indices: { startIndex: number; stopIndex: number }) => void Callback to pass to the onRowsRendered prop of a List. A Grid reports the cells it renders with onCellsRendered instead, so pass along its row indices: function Example({
 columnCount,
 rowCount
}: {
 columnCount: number;
 rowCount: number;
}) {
 const onRowsRendered = useInfiniteLoader({
 isRowLoaded,
 loadMoreRows,
 rowCount
 });

 return (
 <Grid
 cellComponent={CellComponent}
 cellProps={{}}
 columnCount={columnCount}
 columnWidth={100}
 onCellsRendered={({ rowStartIndex, rowStopIndex }) =>
 onRowsRendered({ startIndex: rowStartIndex, stopIndex: rowStopIndex })
 }
 rowCount={rowCount}
 rowHeight={25}
 />
 );
} Continue to InfiniteLoader component…
